{"availability":"available","full":"ccolon/disrupt-sc","name":"disrupt-sc","description":"Spatial agent-based model for simulating supply chain disruptions","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":19,"forks":4,"created":"2022-11-11T10:37:59Z","updated":"2026-10-07T16:51:11Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ccolon.github.io/disrupt-sc/","topics":[],"demo":"https://ccolon.github.io/disrupt-sc/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:37.400Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:37.400Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:37.400Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:31:37.400Z","stars":19,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Spatial agent-based model for supply chain disruption analysis","DisruptSC simulates the economic impact of supply chain disruptions using spatial transport networks, multi-regional input-output data, and agent-based modeling. It analyzes transport infrastructure failures, natural disasters, productivity shocks, and other disruptions across countries and regions.","v2.0 is a major release. The module layout, CLI entry point, and several config keys changed. If you are upgrading from v1, read MIGRATION.md. The legacy v1 line is preserved on the legacy/v1 branch and tagged v1-last-submodule."],"features":["Spatial multimodal transport: roads, rail, maritime, airways, waterways, pipelines","Agent-based economy: firms, households, and countries with spatial disaggregation from MRIO data","Disruption scenarios: transport-edge closures and capacity reductions, cost shocks, capital destruction, productivity shocks","Monte Carlo support: configurable mcrepetitions for disruption and initial-state runs","Input validation: comprehensive data-quality checks before simulation"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ccolon/disrupt-sc/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5ccb465f8a0c0a33175bd967f3151d066178bf1882fe8f0c64112f3ed931f421","extractedAt":"2026-10-07